0,"lift":0.69,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"menorrhagia","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"nosebleed","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":2.87,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"tinea","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.85,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"warts","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":2.68,"evidence_tier":"sparse"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:163-houseleek-or-sengreen":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Houseleek Or Sengreen","headword":"Houseleek Or Sengreen","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"It is an herb of Jupiter, and it is reported by Mezaldus, to preserve what it grows upon from fire and lightning. Our ordinary Houseleek is good for all inward heats as well as outward, and in the eyes or other parts of the body; a posset made with the juice of Houseleek, is singularly good in all hot agues, for it cools and tempers the blood and spirits, and quenches the thirst; and also good to stay all hot defluctions or sharp and salt rheums in the eyes, the juice being dropped into them, or into the ears. It helps also other fluxes of humours in the bowels, and the immoderate courses of women. It cools and restrains all other hot inflammations, St. Anthony’s fire, scaldings and burnings, the shingles, fretting ulcers, cankers, tettors, ringworms, and the like; and much eases the pains of the gout proceeding from any hot cause. The juice also takes away worts and corns in the hands or feet, being often bathed therewith, and the skin and leaves being laid on them afterwards. It eases also the head-ache, and distempered heat of the brain in frenzies, or through want of sleep, being applied to the temples and forehead. The leaves bruised and laid upon the crown or seam of the head, stays bleeding at the nose very quickly. The distilled water of the herb is profitable for all the purposes aforesaid. The leaves being gently rubbed on any place stung with nettles or bees, doth quickly take away the pain.","spans":[{"start":303,"end":308,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":413,"end":461,"concept_id":"conjunctivitis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":536,"end":567,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":577,"end":604,"concept_id":"menorrhagia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":643,"end":656,"concept_id":"inflammation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":662,"end":676,"concept_id":"erysipelas","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":678,"end":687,"concept_id":"burns","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":692,"end":700,"concept_id":"burns","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":706,"end":714,"concept_id":"erysipelas","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":725,"end":731,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":733,"end":740,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":742,"end":749,"concept_id":"dermatitis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":751,"end":760,"concept_id":"tinea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":808,"end":812,"concept_id":"gout","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":870,"end":885,"concept_id":"warts","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1011,"end":1020,"concept_id":"headache","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1059,"end":1067,"concept_id":"delirium","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1080,"end":1093,"concept_id":"insomnia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1208,"end":1228,"concept_id":"nosebleed","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"images":["aeizon-to-mikron-sempervivum-tectorum"]}